From f2e3e1ba8b0111137bddc1869c0c793078b0be97 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oren Teich <oren@teich.net>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 13:38:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Add a Tonal provider on Tonal's unofficial API

Pulls Tonal workouts (title, heart rate, calories and per-set detail in
segments) and the strength score history as health scores in a new
"strength" category, linked to the workout that changed them. Scores
pass 1,000 and health_score.value is numeric(6,3), so value is the
overall score / 10 (qualifier "x10") and components carry the real
overall, upper, lower and core scores.

Tonal has no developer OAuth, so connections are created once with
app.services.providers.tonal.connect (password or email-code grant
against Tonal's Auth0, using the mobile app's public client).

Everything lives in services/providers/tonal; outside it only the
provider and category enums, the factory and the icon change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
